On 13.12.2010 11:57, BanMido wrote:
> 
> Thanks to your very helpful advice, I have cleared Asmodeus, Juiblex
> and Baalzebub quite easily and efficiently.
> This is the first time I have encountered these demon princes and was
> not sure what to expect really. They went down easily, too easily, I
> think.

The bad thing about those demons is that they teleport away to the
up-stairs to completely heal if they are wounded. Though, once you've
blocked their escape route, they can be handled in a straightforward
way. In addition, they respect the E-word, which makes their attacks
easy to counter. A problem - minor, if you're prepared - can be their
summoning; you don't want to face Demogorgon as their companion.

> Minotaurs give a better fight than that was my first thought.

Minotaurs hit very hard, they are fast, and they don't respect the
E-word; that makes them to one of the most dangerous critters in NH.

> That reminds me, are Minotaurs generated in Gehennom? The wiki says
> that they are never generated randomly but I have invariably found at
> least one of them and on most levels, two Minotaurs.

Yes, they are typically  generated in the Gehennom mazes, or in the
maze levels between Medusa and Castle; I usually find either none,
or 1, or 2 minotaurs per level. It's also possible that they appear
in some of the upper dungeon levels (Castle, Ranger's quest, e.g.).

The Wiki may be misleading here; technically speaking, the minotaurs
have the NOGEN flag set which means that they are not generated by
the usual random monster generation process, but their generation is
hard-coded in the mkmaze.c/makemaz() code.

